<!-- SYNTHETIC FIXTURE: fully fictional data (Muster GmbH / DE000000000).
     UBL Invoice, XRechnung 3.0 CIUS, expected VALID (clean) under the German
     profile. This is the SELF-BILLED fixture on the document-TYPE axis
     (T-VHR.26): a BG-25 full-shape body identical in ARITHMETIC to the clean
     full-shape fixture, but issued as a SELF-BILLED invoice — BT-3
     InvoiceTypeCode is 389 (Self-billed invoice, UNTDID 1001) instead of 380.

     WHAT SELF-BILLING IS: in a self-billing (Gutschriftverfahren) arrangement
     the CUSTOMER prepares the invoice on the supplier's behalf; the document is
     still a CrossIndustryInvoice/ubl:Invoice with the same seller and buyer, but
     BT-3 = 389 marks the self-billed nature. XRechnung's BR-DE-17 explicitly
     admits 389 (its allowed BT-3 subset is 326, 380, 384, 389, 381, 875, 876,
     877), and no other XRechnung rule keys on 389, so a self-billed invoice that
     is otherwise full-shape validates CLEAN — exactly like the 380 base. Its
     negative twin (synth-ubl-bad-selfbilled_ubl.xml) swaps 389 for a BT-3 code
     OUTSIDE that subset to make BR-DE-17 fire.

     ARITHMETIC (identical to synth-ubl-good-fullshape, all EUR, consistent):
       BT-106 = 800.00; doc allowance 50.00 (19%), doc charge 30.00 (7%);
       19% base 550.00 -> VAT 104.50; 7% base 230.00 -> VAT 16.10;
       BT-109 = 780.00; BT-110 = 120.60; BT-112 = BT-115 = 900.60 -->
